## 5. Two things this evidence does *not* claim

Stated so the citation is not read as covering more than it does:

- **The plan was written without the probe inputs.** `spec/SAEOS-1.md`, `ledger/` and
  `reviews/tasks/` were not on this stage's read path, so no work unit names a real node type,
  field or goal id. `GAP-1` therefore stands unresolved at plan time (`…:36-37`, `…:513`). The
  plan is executable in the sense that every step is decidable by the executing stage from inputs
  it will hold — not in the sense that its inputs have been seen.
- **The frozen protocol is pinned by line and byte count, not by sha256.** Hashing was not
  permitted in this session, so `wc -lc` (`162 8052`) is the fallback pin and WU-1 carries the
  obligation to compute the real `protocol_sha` at first read, with WU-7 re-verifying it
  (`…:93-98`, `…:271-274`, `PLAN-RISK-1` at `…:515`). A weaker pin stated plainly beats a
  stronger one nobody computed.

